    {
      "gridPos": { "h": 6, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 51 },
      "id": 18,
      "options": {
        "content": "### AI Production & OEE Executive Briefing\n\nAI Production & OEE Analysis is powered by the **Grafana LLM Plugin** (`grafana-llm-app`) querying live PostgreSQL views (`v_current_production_lots`, `v_line_oee_monthly`, `v_asset_oee_components`, `v_filler201_oee_before_after_rca`, `v_shift_staffing_coverage`, `v_shared_asset_risk`, `v_production_schedule_adherence`).\n\n#### Key Production Inquiries Handled:\n- **Current Execution**: *\"What is running on Line 1 right now?\"* → `ATX-20260827-L1-002` (Classic Sauce) at 69.5% completion and 99.00% yield on Shift B.\n- **Next Scheduled Lots**: *\"What lot runs next on Line 2?\"* → `ATX-20260828-L2-001` (BBQ Blend) scheduled for 06:00 on Shift A.\n- **OEE Performance**: *\"Why is Line 2 OEE lower than Line 1?\"* → Line 2 OEE is 86.38% vs. Line 1 at 88.99%, driven almost entirely by **Availability loss** (93.05% vs. 95.67%) from packaging and conveying stops rather than speed or quality.\n- **RCA ROI**: *\"Did Filler-201 improve after RCA?\"* → Filler-201 OEE jumped from **75.71% to 86.31%** (Availability recovered from 83.81% to 95.62%, reducing downtime by 8,278 minutes).\n- **Staffing Coverage**: *\"Is staffing coverage adequate?\"* → Normal coverage on Shift B (1 Lead, 1 L1 Op, 1 L2 Op, 1 Maintenance Tech) adhering to the 1/1/0 rule.\n\n*Run `.\\scripts\\test-ai-summary.ps1` to validate AI responses against OpenAI Base (`gpt-4o-mini`) and Large (`gpt-4o`) models.*",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "title": "AI Production & OEE Decision Support",
      "type": "text"
    }
